    id: "246a1726-8b22-4bf5-8331-5d96efa99778",
    slug: "blackthorn-no-3",
    name: "Blackthorn No. 3",
    description: "The whiskey-based \"Black Thorn\" first appears in Harry Johnson 's 1900 Bartender's Manual . BLACK THORN. (Use a large bar glass.) 3 or 4 dashes of absinthe; 3 or 4 dashes of bitters (Boker's genuine only); \u00bd wine glass of French Vermouth; \u00bd wine glass of Irish Whiskey; Stir up well with a spoon, strain into a medium-sized wine glass and serve. Harry Johnson, Bartender's Manual, 1900 Blackthorn Cocktail. Filla bar glass half full of broken ice and add: 3 dashes of Absinthe. 3 dashes of Angostura Bitters. \u00bc gill of French Vermouth. \u00bc gill of Irish Whiskey. Stir up well with a spoon, strain into a cocktail glass, and squeeze lemon-peel on top. (Recipe by Harry Johnson, of New Orleans.) Robert Vermeire, Cocktails How to Mix Them, 1922 The sloe gin-based version of the Blackthorn appea",
