    name: "Cosmopolitan Delight",
    description: "Adapted from Dale DeGroff 's 2002 book, The Craft of the Cocktail . He, in turn, credits the original recipe to Charlie Paul's 1902 book American and Other Iced Drinks . COSMOPOLITAN DELIGHT. L. D. Take a large soda-water glass and fill with chipped ice; put I a teaspoon of powdered sugar; squeeze half a lemon in; add half a liqueur-glassful of cura\u00e7oa, a teaspoon of orgeat syrup, and half a wine-glassful of brandy; shake well; decorate with fruits in season; dash the top with claret; and serve with straws. Recipes of American and Other Iced Drinks, Charlie Paul, 1902 cosmopolitan delight From Recipes of American and Other Iced Drinks, by Charlie Paul (1902). I included this turn-of-the century Cosmopolitan partly because of the name, but mostly because it tastes great. 1\u00bd ounces",
