    id: "08bbc0a8-9066-4e7d-bc89-f301f549a96f",
    slug: "daiquiri-diffords-recipe",
    name: "Daiquiri (Difford's recipe)",
    description: "My own tried and tested rum-heavy 10 parts rum to 3 parts lime to 2 parts sugar formula. This is my go-to recipe when making a straight-up Daiquiri with a dry light white (charcoal-filtered) rum. When using a more full-bodied rum, I follow a 6:2:1 Daiquiri recipe, which is better suited to \"golden\" rums . Being the original Daiquiri, it is appropriately called Daiquiri No. 1 and is also known in Cuba as a \"Natural Daiquiri,\" referring to its being shaken rather than blended. This is the first of four numbered daiquiris in the 1934 1st edition Bar La Florida Cocktails , menu book of the famous El Floridita Bar , Havana, Cuba. Daiquiri Num. 1 2 Ounces Bacard\u00ed Rum. 1 Teaspoonful Sugar. Juice of half a lemon. Cracked ice. Shake well and strain into cocktail glass. Bar La Florida Cockt",
