    name: "Godfather Cocktail",
    description: "The Godfather is one of the enduring classics to emerge from the 1970s. It's basically an Old-Fashioned with attitude \u2013 the attitude being: why sweeten with mere sugar when you can use a flavoursome liqueur. The appearance of the whole 'God damn' cocktail family in Stanley M. Jones' 1977 Jones' Complete Barguide , and numerous cocktail books from the 1980s, is testament to the Godfather being a 1970s cocktail . Indeed, this cocktail is eponymously named after the Italian-American Mafia book and film trilogy, The Godfather . Mario Puzo's novel was published in 1969 and Francis Ford Coppola's first film followed in March 1972, the highest-grossing film of the year, and for some years after. The earliest recipe book mention of the Godfather (and also the Godmother and French Connecti",
